a pre-print hang: a probe of the same early path at main 981a45802 (same queue, same mandate) timed git fetch 2.0s, `required()` 0.9s, first poll 3.6s, then sat in `main_green`'s required-only wait at main's tip and emitted `beat: waiting CI at 981a4580 (poll 2, t+305s, required: 14, concluded: 11/14)` — a healthy FULL run in progress. The beats existed but never reached the log: the wrapper's dup2 makes stdout a file and Python block-buffers a file, so every line sat in an 8KB buffer the SIGKILL dropped. Secondary: the beat is poll-gated — `POLL_SECONDS` (300) behind `HEARTBEAT_SECONDS` (240) held the first beat to t+305s, so even unbuffered the log was blank for the first 5 minutes. Three one-liners kill the class: the entry reconfigures stdout line-buffered (the instrument is self-sufficient, not reliant on a launcher flag); batch and train announce themselves as the first line (tag, pid, base, queue) before any blocking call; and wait_ci's poll sleeps only until the next beat is due.\n\n## Head\n\n10e225062b9af74ad94fcafb8cc1c34fe681e14e (branch fix/train-silent-launch, base origin/main 981a45802dce96b3d43d07068384f7944f58eb35; evidence dir /private/tmp/r9-ev-trainfix/HEAD-EVIDENCE.txt)\n\n## Mutation proof\n\nEach new arm was reddened by reverting exactly its own fix, one at a time, then restored:\n\n- revert `main()`'s `sys.stdout.reconfigure(line_buffering=True)` → `FAIL the entry point reconfigures stdout line-buffered before reading the queue, so a redirected launch's beats reach the log as they print` (138 checks, 1 failed)\n- delete the batch banner → `FAIL batch announces itself in its FIRST line -- tag, pid, base, the queue's PRs -- before any blocking call, so a daemonized launch is attributable from the log's first line` (138 checks, 1 failed)\n- revert the sleep to `self.sleep(POLL_SECONDS)` → `FAIL a beat is never held behind a poll boundary: the poll sleeps to the next beat, so beats land at t+240 and t+480 (not t+300/t+600 behind POLL_SECONDS)` (138 checks, 1 failed)\n\nAll three reverts restored: 138 checks, 0 failed.\n\n## Null control\n\nThe unmodified tree at the same head: the self-test's pre-existing heartbeat arms pass unchanged (the two stubbed-clock arms consume one clock read per poll under both sleeps), and the batch null control (two clean PRs proved once and both merged) passes — the banner and sleep change no gate, return value or wait duration. The 135 pre-existing checks were green before the fix and after it.\n\n## Figures\n\n- `python3 tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py --self-test` → 135 checks, 0 failed before; 138 checks, 0 failed after (three new arms).\n- `python3 /private/tmp/r9-ev-trainfix/probe.py` (read-only early path at main 981a45802, real repo) → git fetch 2.0s, required 0.9s, first poll 3.6s; beat `beat: waiting CI at 981a4580 (poll 2, t+305s, required: 14, concluded: 11/14)` at t+308s (log /private/tmp/r9-ev-trainfix/probe.log).\n- rehearsal under the incident's exact wrapper shape (`/private/tmp/r9-ev-trainfix/launch-rehearse.py` — fork/setsid/dup2 to a file, execvp python3 with no `-u`, byte-identical shape to tonight's `/private/tmp/r9-ev-trainfix/launch-traintest.py`): `BATCH rehearse pid=17100 base=batch/rehearse-silent queue=1 (#2066) --overlap --skip-bad` is the log's first line at t+0 and the whole run (SKIP REPORT, TRAIN DONE) is legible at t+15s (log /private/tmp/r9-ev-trainfix/rehearse.log); tonight's log /private/tmp/r9-ev-trainfix/traintest.log held 40 bytes for 8+ minutes.\n- forced under-queued wait, same wrapper shape (`/private/tmp/r9-ev-trainfix/launch-wait2.py`): `python3 tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py wait-ci --min-runs 15 903283a394560d6cb516481debdde2dcf47c6ade` — beats appeared in the log at **t+241s** (`beat: waiting CI at 903283a3 (poll 2, t+241s, required: 0, concluded: 0/0)`) and **t+481s** (poll 3, t+481s), each sampled in real time at the 240s mark (log /private/tmp/r9-ev-trainfix/wait2.log). The old code's first beat lands at t+305s (measured, probe.log).\n- `python3 tests/structure.py` → STRUCTURE RATCHET PASSED, no budget moved.\n\n## Red checks\n\nfast (3.14) reds in this branch's history are main's two main-data defects fixed by #2173 (the branch carries no data change), and the delivery-status red is main's row debt being cleared by the beat now the #2176 rewrite guard has landed; neither touches this diff, which changes logging only.\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone\n\n## Friction\n\n- none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T23:26:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T02:01:38Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T02:01:36Z","merged_at":"2026-10-14T02:01:36Z","merge_commit_sha":"d9e54b6420dffadd62a3490f3295277bce03f74b","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2180/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2180/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2180/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/10e225062b9af74ad94fcafb8cc1c34fe681e14e","head":{"label":"tvofi:fix/train-silent-launch","ref":"fix/train-silent-launch","sha":"10e225062b9af74ad94fcafb8cc1c34fe681e14e","user":{"login":"tvofi","id":70032254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMDMyMjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tvofi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"http